cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "attribution-graph: evidence-ranked entity resolution for attribution investigations"
message: "If you use this software or the method it implements, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Karumudi
    # Add your ORCID before release; it makes the work
    # machine-linkable to you across citation systems.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    given-names: Tushar
repository-code: "https://github.com/tusharkarumudi/attribution-graph"
abstract: >-
  A log-likelihood-ratio evidence model for deciding whether observed
  identifiers denote the same real-world entity. Evidence weight is derived
  from measured corpus selectivity rather than hand-tuned weights; correlated
  observations are deduplicated by correlation group; and a group cap set below
  the prior enforces corroboration structurally rather than by convention.
  Includes per-predicate temporal decay, must-not-link constraints for
  inter-entity relations, and ICD 203 estimative reporting.
keywords:
  - open source intelligence
  - entity resolution
  - record linkage
  - attribution
  - threat intelligence
license: Apache-2.0
version: 2.0.2
